 [{:section/type :communication-multiplied
   :section/id 7
   :section/title "I want to see her this weekend"
   :section/body
   ["Quiero verla este fin de semana Remember for this week we said Esta semana And for next week we said La próxima semana Many feminine words in Spanish end with the letter a."
    "Semana ends with the letter a and is a feminine word."
    "Mes and Año (month and year) are masculine words."
    "To say this with Masculine words use este."
    "This year Este año This month Este mes And to say the next with masculine words, use el próximo."
    "The next year El próximo año The next month El próximo mes Something to remember about the weekend Semana - Week is feminine but Fin de semana - Weekend is masculine Therefore, how would you make the following phrases?"
    "1. Next week 2. Next weekend 3. This week 4. This weekend Check your answer below. Then when you do exercise 6B notice the use of este and el próximo."
    "Answers 1. la próxima semana, 2. el próximo fin de semana, 3. esta semana, 4.este fin de semana"]}]
